; Invalid: a `(pass …)` whose WGSL names `controls`, in a document that declares
; no `(control …)`. `controls` is the prelude's controls binding (frame-program
; §4.5) — the same rule that binds `pngine`/`pointer`/`samp` when the pass's own
; text names them — and with nothing declared there is no struct to declare, no
; buffer to bind, and no value the host could ever set. Declare a control:
;
;   (control :name warp :default 0.5)
;   (pass-graph
;     (pass :name main :code """
;       @fragment fn fs(@builtin(position) pos: vec4f) -> @location(0) vec4f {
;         return vec4f(vec3f(controls.warp), 1.0);
;       }
;     """))
;
; …or rename the variable. In a document that DOES declare a control, `controls`
; is reserved exactly here and nowhere else, so no existing document changes (D5).

(pass-graph
  (pass :name main :code """
    @fragment fn fs(@builtin(position) pos: vec4f) -> @location(0) vec4f {
      return vec4f(vec3f(controls.warp), 1.0);
    }
  """))
